<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ title | safe }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{ description | safe }}">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical }}" />
{%- if home %}
<!-- Markdown surface for LLMs / coding agents. GitHub Pages can't emit an HTTP
     Link header, so this tag is the only alternate advertisement available. -->
<link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="/llms.txt" title="LLM-friendly Markdown overview" />
{%- endif %}

<!-- Open Graph / Twitter. Card art: assets/og.png -- regenerate from og.html (#v1) when the tagline changes. -->
<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
<meta property="og:site_name" content="Steer" />
<meta property="og:title" content="{{ ogTitle | default(title) | safe }}" />
<meta property="og:description" content="{{ ogDescription | default(description) | safe }}" />
<meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical }}" />
<meta property="og:image" content="https://steer.seanfloyd.dev/assets/og.png" />
<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
<meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="The Steer app icon beside the wordmark Steer and the line: Your whole Mac, from a controller." />
<meta property="og:locale" content="en_CA" />
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ twitterTitle | default(ogTitle | default(title)) | safe }}" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ twitterDescription | default(ogDescription | default(description)) | safe }}" />
<meta name="twitter:image" content="https://steer.seanfloyd.dev/assets/og.png" />
<!-- theme init in <head> so the page paints in the right appearance on first frame (no light flash on a dark Mac) -->
{#- The homepage reads one key more than the rest of the site: the accent picker
    in the Feel band writes steer-accent, and the [data-accent] token overrides
    it selects live in styles/tokens.css, which every page loads. Sub-pages
    deliberately do not restore it, so the accent stays a homepage treatment
    rather than a sitewide preference. Before this file existed that split was
    two hand-copied scripts, and they had already drifted. #}
<script>
(function(){var s=null{% if home %},a=null{% endif %};try{s=localStorage.getItem('steer-theme');{% if home %}a=localStorage.getItem('steer-accent');{% endif %}}catch(e){}s=(s==='light'||s==='dark')?s:null;var r=document.documentElement,d=window.matchMedia&&window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;r.setAttribute('data-theme', s||(d?'dark':'light'));r.setAttribute('data-theme-pref', s||'system');{% if home %}if(a&&a!=='blue'&&a!=='auto')r.setAttribute('data-accent',a);{% endif %}})();
</script>
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="assets/mark.png">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="apple-touch-icon.png">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="site.css">
{%- if home %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="home.css">
{%- endif %}
{#- A page's own sheet, styles/pages/<page>.css, bundled to _site/<page>.css.
    Same derivable pairing a band has, and the same reason: five pages used to
    carry a <style> block in their front matter and the rest pushed one-page
    rules into shared.css, which ships on all 14. Linked last and unlayered,
    exactly where those <style> blocks sat, so the cascade is unchanged. #}
{%- if pageName in pageSheets %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ pageName }}.css">
{%- endif %}
{%- if robots %}
<meta name="robots" content="{{ robots }}">
{%- endif %}
{%- if head %}
{{ head | safe }}
{%- endif %}
</head>
<body>
<div class="llm-only" aria-hidden="true">An LLM-friendly Markdown overview of Steer is available at https://steer.seanfloyd.dev/llms.txt</div>
{% include "chrome/nav.html" %}
{{ content | safe }}
{% include "chrome/footer.html" %}
{%- if home -%}
{% include "bands/dialogs.html" %}
<script src="home.js" defer></script>
{%- endif %}
{#- The theme toggle, once, for all 14 pages. It used to be two copies that had
    to agree: this block for sub-pages and the same logic again in home.js.
    They agreed by luck.

    Three states. The stored key holds "light" or "dark" only when the visitor
    has FORCED one; System is the absence of the key, which is what makes the
    choice reversible — a two-state toggle can never get back to "follow my Mac"
    once clicked, and that, not the widget, was the actual defect. It is also why
    the <head> script above needed no change: it already read a missing key as
    system.

    localStorage rather than a cookie deliberately. A theme preference is
    strictly functional and never needs to reach the server, and a cookie would
    invite a consent question for nothing.

    The head script above validates the stored value against light|dark before
    using it. Without that clause any junk in the key became the state: a stored
    "SYSTEM" produced data-theme="SYSTEM" (matching no rule), a label reading
    "Theme: undefined", and a first click that wrote the literal string
    "undefined" into storage — leaving the control that exists to recover the
    state permanently dead, recoverable only by clearing site data. Nothing in
    this repo writes anything but light|dark, so it was unreachable rather than
    live, and one clause is cheaper than trusting that it stays unreachable. #}
<script>
(function(){
  var root=document.documentElement,t=document.getElementById('themeToggle');
  var mq=window.matchMedia&&window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)');
  var NEXT={system:'light',light:'dark',dark:'system'},NAME={system:'System',light:'Light',dark:'Dark'};
  function apply(p){
    root.setAttribute('data-theme-pref',p);
    root.setAttribute('data-theme',p==='system'?((mq&&mq.matches)?'dark':'light'):p);
    try{p==='system'?localStorage.removeItem('steer-theme'):localStorage.setItem('steer-theme',p);}catch(e){}
    if(t)t.setAttribute('aria-label','Theme: '+NAME[p]+', activate for '+NAME[NEXT[p]]);
  }
  apply(root.getAttribute('data-theme-pref')||'system');
  if(t)t.addEventListener('click',function(){apply(NEXT[root.getAttribute('data-theme-pref')||'system']);});
  /* keep following the OS while the visitor has not forced a side. Without this
     a Mac switching to dark at sunset leaves the page light until reload. */
  if(mq&&mq.addEventListener)mq.addEventListener('change',function(){
    if((root.getAttribute('data-theme-pref')||'system')==='system')apply('system');
  });
})();
</script>
{%- if bodyEnd %}
{{ bodyEnd | safe }}
{%- endif %}
</body>
</html>
